meta {
  name: delete document
  type: http
  seq: 5
}

delete {
  url: {{base_url}}/v1/documents/{{document_id}}
  body: none
  auth: inherit
}

docs {
  PRD §6.6. Removes the document from both stores — the row from PostgreSQL and
  the vectors from Chroma.

  **Idempotent.** `204` whether or not the document existed, which is what makes
  a retry safe: a client that timed out mid-delete cannot tell which side of the
  vector purge it stopped on. The `X-Deleted` header reports which of the two
  happened, for a caller that wants to know; the status deliberately does not.

  Requires the `write` scope, so the n8n key cannot run this — see
  `99-negative/delete without the write scope`.

  Run this last: it removes the document the other requests in this folder use.
}

assert {
  res.status: eq 204
}
